<Layout
  title="About | Darren R. Skidmore"
  description="Learn more about Darren Skidmore."
>
  <h1>About Me</h1>
  <section class="stack">
    <p>
      I have been studying Computer Science at <a href="https://byu.edu/"
        >Brigham Young University (BYU)</a
      > in Provo, Utah since August 2022. My major includes an emphasis in data science
      and minors in statistics and mathematics. Prior to my education at BYU, I received
      an AAS in Computer Science from <a href="https://weber.edu/"
        >Weber State University</a
      > in April 2022. I have always strongly valued education and I am grateful for
      the educators in my life who have inspired and supported me.
    </p>
    <p>
      I have held a variety of technical-related jobs since 2020, including my
      current position as a QA Engineer for the <a href="https://oit.byu.edu/"
        >Office of Information Technology (OIT)</a
      > at Brigham Young University, working as a research assistant in BYU's <a
        href="https://imaal.byu.edu/"
        >Internet Measurement and Anti-Abuse Laboratory</a
      >, and holding software engineering, data visualization, and technical
      support responsibilities for <a
        href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/"
        >the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints</a
      > as a full-time <a
        href="https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/service-missionary"
        >missionary</a
      >.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some of my other interests are running, hiking, photography, vinyl
      collecting (particularly downtempo and trip-hop) and keeping up with data
      blogs (my favorites right now include <a
        href="https://www.natesilver.net/">Nate Silver</a
      >, <a href="https://substack.com/@ryanburge">Ryan Burge</a>, and <a
        href="https://substack.com/@acbass49">Alex Bass</a
      >.)
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
